## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of MVCC, anomalies, and cross-batch correctness in a high-concurrency payout workflow.

## Key Concepts
- MVCC, SERIALIZABLE, SSI
- Row-level locking, SELECT FOR UPDATE
- Idempotent writes, upserts, optimistic locking, version/timestamp columns
- Long-running transactions and abort rates

## Code Example
```sql
BEGIN;
SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;
SELECT balance, version FROM drivers WHERE id = :driver_id FOR UPDATE;
-- compute new_balance using :amount and existing balance/version
UPDATE drivers SET balance = new_balance, version = version + 1 WHERE id = :driver_id;
INSERT INTO payout_ledger(driver_id, amount, tstamp) VALUES (:driver_id, :amount, NOW());
COMMIT;
```

